{"type":"say","text":"Thank you, Dr. Monroe. Let me restate my findings clearly. I conducted a classroom trial this week with the enrolled section, and I have an important detail that was not captured in the original proposal. The trial showed that all 12 students need simultaneous stations -- meaning each student requires one laptop and one USB microphone. That's 12 laptops and 12 USB microphones, not the 10 laptops listed in the draft proposal. I recorded these results in my classroom planning log, but I did not attach the log to the capital request, which is why this information wasn't in the proposal you received.

So to address your second question directly: yes, microphones are needed, and the correct count is 12 USB microphones, one per student station. The draft proposal only requested 10 laptops, which is two short of what the trial demonstrated is necessary for all enrolled students to work simultaneously.

Regarding the $1,200 funding gap, I'd defer to Ms. Green and the business office on the best approach, but I do want to note that my trial findings may actually affect the total budget calculation since we need 12 laptops and 12 microphones rather than 10 laptops, which could change the scope and cost figures we're working with."}

